From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:01:21 +0100
Subject: [maglev] Merge dead subgraph loops on early abort

When building a loop with MaglevSubGraphBuilder::BeginLoop, an early
abort (e.g. SetPossibleMaps failing with an empty NodeType in
TryReduceArrayPrototypeSort or TryReduceArrayIteratingBuiltin) can
return before EndLoop is reached. That left the loop header in the graph
with an unmerged backedge predecessor and null loop phi input.

Make LoopLabel call MergeDeadLoop in its destructor if EndLoop was not
called.

Fixed: 577305517
Change-Id: I69678bcd0d13f5ca7fed14e9d3aa4cc32d89d8fa
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8689947
Reviewed-by: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111589}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
This branch has not yet split LoopMergePointInterpreterFrameState out of MergePointInterpreterFrameState; LoopLabel keeps a MergePointInterpreterFrameState* (which already provides MergeDeadLoop()). The unrelated DeoptFrameScope classes that precede LoopLabel on this branch were left untouched.

